+/*
+ * Composite personality (sweetusb>=5): ONE configuration that carries BOTH the
+ * usbmux/iAP2 function and the CDC-NCM function.  That is what gate C0 asks
+ * for, and it is the one thing the two existing personalities cannot do:
+ * UD_APPLE advertises only 05ac:12a8 FF/FE/02 and UD_NCM only 1209:0001
+ * 02/0D/00, so a host sees either iAP2 or NCM, never both.
+ *
+ * Interface 0 is descriptor-identical to the UD_APPLE function (FF/FE/02, the
+ * bulk pair 0x81/0x01) and the device keeps Apple's 05ac:12a8 with a product
+ * id inside usbmuxd's 0x1290..0x12af window, so usbmuxd still binds the mux
+ * function.  Interfaces 1 and 2 are the CDC-NCM function: control interface 1
+ * (02/0D/00) with the 16-byte interrupt endpoint 0x83, data interface 2
+ * (0A/00/01) with alt 0/alt 1 and the bulk pair 0x84/0x02.  The functional
+ * descriptors are the same bytes as the UD_NCM set; only the interface numbers,
+ * the endpoint addresses and the notification wIndex differ.
+ *
+ * Endpoint addresses follow the DWC3 2n = OUT / 2n+1 = IN rule, so the physical
+ * endpoints are 0x81 -> ep3 and 0x01 -> ep2 (mux, reused from UD_APPLE) plus
+ * 0x83 -> ep7, 0x84 -> ep9 and 0x02 -> ep4 (NCM, new).  The NCM function gets
+ * its own TRBs and DMA buffers (UD_TRB_NCM_*, UD_NCM_*) so mux frames and NCM
+ * NTBs can be in flight at the same time without sharing a buffer.
+ */
+#define UD_CARPLAY      3
